    {
      "name": "6 \u00b7 Sign up a PARTICIPANT through my link",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Cookie",
            "value": "trybe_ref={{refCode}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "http://127.0.0.1:1048/api/v1/auth/register",
          "protocol": "http",
          "host": [
            "127",
            "0",
            "0",
            "1"
          ],
          "port": "1048",
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "auth",
            "register"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Deliberately the wrong role. It gets recorded and shown, but it will report counts_towards_reward = false, because the reward is defined only for matching pairs. Without that flag a page could read \"3 of 3\" and pay nothing.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n    \"name\": \"Demo Friend 4\",\n    \"email\": \"demo.participant4@trybe.test\",\n    \"phone\": \"01790004004\",\n    \"password\": \"password123\",\n    \"password_confirmation\": \"password123\",\n    \"role\": \"participant\",\n    \"location\": \"Dhaka, Bangladesh\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7 \u00b7 Progress BEFORE they do anything",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "http://127.0.0.1:1048/api/v1/referrals/me",
          "protocol": "http",
          "host": [
            "127",
            "0",
            "0",
            "1"
          ],
          "port": "1048",
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "referrals",
            "me"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Four referrals recorded, ZERO qualified. Signing up is not enough \u2014 that is the main defence against fake accounts.\n\nNOW RUN THIS IN A TERMINAL:\n\n  php artisan trybe:demo:qualify --referrer=sarah.researcher@trybe.test --no-sync\n\nIt posts a first study for each referred researcher and completes one for the referred participant \u2014 the real actions that qualify them. It does NOT set status=qualified and grants nothing; sync() draws that conclusion in step 8."
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
              "console.log('=========================================');",
              "console.log(' ' + d.progress.label);",
              "console.log(' qualified        : ' + d.progress.qualified_count);",
              "console.log(' counts to reward : ' + d.progress.eligible_count +",
              "            '/' + d.progress.required_to_unlock);",
              "console.log(' still pending    : ' + d.progress.pending_count);",
              "console.log(' rewards          : ' + d.rewards.length);",
              "console.log('=========================================');",
              "d.referred_users.forEach(function (p) {",
              "    console.log('  ' + p.name + '  ' + p.status_label +",
              "                (p.counts_towards_reward ? '' : '   <- different role, does not count'));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "8 \u00b7 SYNC  \u2014 the reward fires",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "http://127.0.0.1:1048/api/v1/referrals/me/sync",
          "protocol": "http",
          "host": [
            "127",
            "0",
            "0",
            "1"
          ],
          "port": "1048",
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "referrals",
            "me",
            "sync"
          ]
        },
        "description": "granted_now = 1. sync() re-reads live study data, flips the three researcher referrals to qualified, counts 3 eligible, and grants the milestone reward inside a transaction.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log('granted_now = ' + j.granted_now +",
              "  (j.granted_now ? '   <-- REWARD FIRED' : '   <-- already granted, idempotent'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "9 \u00b7 SYNC AGAIN \u2014 idempotency",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "http://127.0.0.1:1048/api/v1/referrals/me/sync",
          "protocol": "http",
          "host": [
            "127",
            "0",
            "0",
            "1"
          ],
          "port": "1048",
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "referrals",
            "me",
            "sync"
          ]
        },
        "description": "granted_now = 0. Nothing is granted twice. That is enforced by unique(user_id, type, milestone) in the database, not by an if-statement \u2014 which is why it also holds if two requests race.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": [],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "console.log('granted_now = ' + j.granted_now +",
              "  (j.granted_now ? '   <-- REWARD FIRED' : '   <-- already granted, idempotent'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
